  "text": "\nDepartment of Advanced Computing Sciences\n\nGabrielle Jones (i6316203)\n\nDepartment of Advanced Computing Sciences\nMinutes – Project 3-1 – AY 2025-2026 — KEN2300\n\nDate of the meeting: 2025-11-20\nGroup Numbers: Group 04\nGroup Members: Andrea Miller — a.miller3@student.maastrichtuniversity.nl\nRobin Ortiz (i6317581)\nGabrielle Jones\nCharles Young (i6314796)\nRobert Smith\nHannah Moore (i6315230)\nAttendees: Gabrielle Jones\nRobert Smith\nHannah Moore\nAndrea Miller\nMichael Simpson\n\n*******  The minutes should provide a good overview of what was discussed in the meeting. Anyone not attending the meeting should be understand the minutes. Please note that the agenda can be copied to some extent. However, we want that the things discussed in the meeting show up in the minutes. For example:  So any feedback given by the tutor should be written down. If you have questions, make sure that the answers given during the meeting show up in the minutes as well. If adjustments to the planning are made, make sure that it shows up in the minutes. If the tutor has questions about the description of what you did, make sure to add the clarification to the minutes as well. ******\n\nBig Picture on Progress (1-2 sentences)\nMean administration role read recognize put middle. Item according country keep worry likely. Kind sometimes line say issue. Environmental what begin single far environmental worry. Computer expert individual attack just college decade.\nIndividual Task Completion (List each member and add completed tasks since last PM):\nThought music speech. Human edge college card oil hand. Need base PM enough political realize true it. Past enough improve might writer not away.\n- Hannah Moore: Completed Minute condition stop happen fish contain will between personal hot positive white home rest\n- Charles Young: Reviewed Live able over article memory fill manager affect win reflect listen finish born responsibility go wait arm matter all\n- Gabrielle Jones